Title:
Auditing in the age of “good enough” AI (Miden zkVM case study)

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Trail of Bits describes how “agentic” AI is used before and during audits to build bespoke tooling and formal models that increase review depth, not just to do automated code review.  
- The case study is an audit of the Miden zkVM core library, written in Miden Assembly (MASM), a stack-based custom ISA with minimal existing developer tooling.  
- Over ~6 months, agents helped build a MASM LSP/VS Code extension, a decompiler with an IR, a static analysis engine (including abstract interpretation), and a Lean model + MASM→Lean translation pipeline.  
- The tooling surfaced >400 type/validation hardening findings and a high-severity bug: an underconstrained prover-supplied “advice” remainder in `mod_12289` enabling incorrect modular reduction and potential Falcon signature forgery leading to fund theft.  
- Formal methods work produced 95 machine-checked correctness proofs and also uncovered subtle arithmetic/stack-manipulation bugs missed by unit tests.  
- Useful for security auditors, ZK/crypto engineers, and both red/blue teams working on high-assurance VM/DSL ecosystems where tooling gaps block effective review.

Technical Focus:
- Stack-machine ISA auditing (MASM) and stack-effect tracking
- Language Server Protocol (LSP) tooling + VS Code integration for custom languages
- Decompilation/lifting to an intermediate representation (IR) for analysis
- Static analysis passes and abstract interpretation for type/constraint validation
- ZKVM “advice” inputs (prover-supplied values) and constraint soundness
- Formal verification in Lean (machine-checked proofs, MASM→Lean translation)

Use Cases:
- Build audit-grade tooling for new VMs/DSLs lacking IDE support and analyzers
- Detect underconstrained prover inputs in ZK systems (advice/auxiliary witnesses)
- Automate type/width/boolean constraint enforcement checks in low-level crypto code
- Generate decompilation/IR to enable dataflow analysis and lints for stack languages
- Produce machine-checked correctness proofs for critical arithmetic primitives

Keywords:
Trail of Bits, Miden VM, zkVM, zero-knowledge, MASM, stack machine, advice stack, prover-supplied input, constraint validation, Falcon signatures, modular reduction, `mod_12289`, decompiler, IR lifting, static analysis, abstract interpretation, LSP, VS Code extension, Lean, formal verification, correctness proofs, dataflow analysis, linter